[FINAL-TEXT] **Root cause found.** Router6's nftables FORWARD chain has an explicit, broad DROP rule blocking **all traffic arriving on eth2** (the WAN/uplink interface toward router3):

```
iifname "eth2" ip saddr 172.16.10.0/24 ip daddr 172.18.51.1 tcp dport 80 accept  ← narrow exception
iifname "eth2" meta l4proto tcp  drop   ← drops all TCP from WAN
iifname "eth2" meta l4proto udp  drop   ← drops all UDP from WAN
iifname "eth2"                   drop   ← drops everything else (ICMP, etc.)
```

The traceroute from PC15 confirms: hop 1 (router6 gateway) responds, then all further hops are `* * *` — every return packet from outside hits this filter and is discarded. Router6 pinging PC11 works because locally-generated traffic bypasses the FORWARD chain entirely (it uses the INPUT chain for replies). PC15 pinging its own gateway works because that is L2-local and never transits eth2.

